      "body": "## Motivation\n\nFixes #39886.\n\nDSpark explicitly supports DP attention with a DeepSeek-V4/MoE draft when attention TP size is 1 and full TP size is greater than 1. In that configuration `DSparkWorkerV2` constructs `SpecTpSync` with the singleton `attn_tp_group` (correct for runtime broadcasts: peer DP ranks run different requests) while draft CUDA graph capture uses the larger `tp_group`.\n\nThe memory probe already passes that capture group to `SpecTpSync.available_memory_gb`, but the constructor had cleared every sync site because its group had one rank. The helper therefore read rank-local free memory instead of reducing the minimum over full TP. If those readings fall on opposite sides of the 1 GiB decode-graph cutoff, some ranks skip capture while others enter it and hit `tp_group` barriers in `FullCudaGraphBackend.capture_one`, which can stall startup.\n\nThe unit reproduction in the issue is the skipped reduction (`distributed=False` for a 2-rank override group). A multi-GPU hang was not reproduced here; it follows from the mismatched collective participation.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Keep the configured `SGLANG_SPEC_TP_SYNC` site set on `SpecTpSync` even when the constructor broadcast group is a singleton.\n- Reduce `available_memory_gb` over the caller-supplied group when that site is configured and `group.world_size > 1`.\n- Leave `sync()` on the constructor group so DP-attention runtime broadcasts stay inside attn-TP.\n- Add a CPU unit test for the attn-TP=1 / full-TP>1 memory probe, site-off, multi-rank constructor, and the still-disabled runtime broadcast.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nN/A — startup memory consensus only; no change to model outputs.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the Format code with pre-commit.\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the Run and add unit tests.\n- [ ] Update documentation according to Write documentations.\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to Test the accuracy and Benchmark the speed.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style guidance.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #35210912220](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35210912220)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35210912062](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35210912062)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35210912238](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35210912238)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
